  "einstBackupVerschluesseln": "Encrypt backup",
  "einstBackupPassphraseAbfrage": "Asks for the backup passphrase above when needed.",
  "einstBackupZielWaehlen": "Choose a backup destination (e.g. your Dropbox or Google Drive folder)",
  "einstBackupOrdnerWaehlen": "Choose the backup folder (the one containing “PhotoVault-Backup” or “originals”)",
  "einstBackupEntschluesselnTitel": "Turn off backup encryption?",
  "einstBackupEntschluesselnText": "New backups will no longer be encrypted. Encrypted backups already at the destination stay as they are and remain decryptable only with the previous passphrase.",
  "einstBackupLaeuft": "Automatic backup running …",
  "einstBackupKeineNeuen": "No new files – refreshing the database snapshot.",
  "einstBackupZielHinweis": "Point this at your local Dropbox or Google Drive folder, for instance – that provider's desktop app then uploads the files to the cloud for you.",
  "einstBackupAutoHinweis": "Runs only while the app is open (there is no background service) – it checks at start-up and every 30 minutes afterwards whether the interval has elapsed. Always encrypted, and alongside the original files it saves a snapshot of the whole database (faces, places, tags, albums, favourites, …) so the complete state can be restored after data loss. It never deletes anything at the destination – local deletions are deliberately not mirrored.",
  "einstBackupZuerstZiel": "Choose a destination folder first.",
  "einstBackupKeinOrdner": "No folder chosen.",
  "einstBackupAutoZielWaehlen": "Choose the destination for automatic backups",
  "einstWaehlen": "Choose…",
